      "headline": "Brazil Central Bank FX Official: Converting Legitimate Funds Into Stablecoins Gives Them a “Dirty Money” Label and Constitutes Money Laundering Gerson Romantini, head of the Central Bank of Brazil’s foreign exchange division, said at a closed-door event that legitimate funds acquire a “dirty money” label when converted into stablecoins and are then considered money laundering, according to Livecoins. He said the central bank is particularly concerned about stablecoins’ role in remittances. The report noted that fintech companies’ practice of receiving reais, converting them into stablecoins and transferring them to overseas companies for payments or family remittances was prohibited under Resolution No. 561/2026, which took effect on Oct. 1. — link",
